; npm ci refuses to install this lockfile without this.
;
; The tree is internally inconsistent on peer dependencies, and always has been:
;
;   @angular/cli ~21.2.7      vs  @angular-eslint/* ^22.1.0  (wants CLI >= 22)
;   eslint ^10.9.1            vs  eslint-plugin-import ^2.32  (wants eslint <= 9)
;   jasmine-core ~3.4         vs  karma-jasmine-html-reporter (wants >= 3.8)
;
; The installed versions work — the unit and E2E suites and the linter all pass on
; them — so npm's strict peer resolution is rejecting a tree that is known good.
; Aligning the versions instead means upgrading the Angular 21 framework or the
; Jasmine/Karma test toolchain, which is a much larger change than the peer
; warnings justify, and would invalidate a verified test suite.
;
; Remove this file when those version families are aligned deliberately.
legacy-peer-deps=true
